change:
  id: CHG-006
  title: Harness-agnostic agent invocation boundary
  status: proposed
  intent: Introduce a provider- and harness-neutral invocation contract so Goose, OpenCode, Codex, Claude, direct APIs and local processes can be swapped behind adapters while SAAA retains routing, isolation, evidence, evaluation and promotion authority.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - SYS-001
    - ARCH-001
    - ADR-0002
    - ADR-0003
    - Q-010
    - RISK-001

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: agent-harness-boundary
    requirement: SAAA exposes a provider-neutral AgentHarness port accepting a bounded request and returning structured invocation evidence; external harnesses and model providers remain adapter concerns.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: an agent invocation is prepared
        then: the request contains the mutation proposal, isolated workspace, capability allowlist, expected output schema, selected route and remaining resource budget
        and:
          - route selection is explicit and auditable before invocation
          - token, credit, wall-clock and retry limits cannot be negative
          - an adapter rejects an invocation whose input-token, output-token or wall-clock allowance is exhausted
      - id: S2
        when: a harness returns
        then: the result identifies completion, failure, timeout or rejection and records provider-neutral usage and optional session/output references
        and:
          - a completed result contains a mutation
          - a non-completed result contains no mutation
      - id: S3
        when: an existing proposer is exposed through the compatibility adapter
        then: successful proposals become completed harness results and proposer failures become failed results without approval
        and:
          - no provider-specific dependency enters domain or deterministic
          - deterministic evaluation remains the authority after the harness returns

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: domain/AgentRequestTest.rejectsNegativeResourceBudget
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: domain/AgentRequestTest.requiresCompletedResultToCarryAMutation
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: adapters/evolve/MutationProposerAgentHarnessTest.exposesSuccessfulLegacyProposerAsAuditedCompletedRun
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: adapters/evolve/MutationProposerAgentHarnessTest.capturesProposalFailureWithoutApprovingIt
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: add provider-neutral route, budget, usage, request and result records
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: add the deterministic AgentHarness port and legacy proposer compatibility adapter
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: document the harness-agnostic architecture and preserve the deterministic approval boundary
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: add ACP, OpenCode, Goose, Codex and Claude adapters after the neutral contract has measured use
    status: pending

non_goals:
  - implementing another general-purpose agent product
  - putting ACP, MCP, CLI, provider or vendor types in the core boundary
  - changing mutation validation, fitness weights, thresholds or promotion semantics
  - routing by opaque model-name heuristics before resource-aware ablation evidence exists
  - implementing ethical or personal-preference routing in this boundary slice; Q-011 captures that follow-up

risks:
  - the compatibility adapter currently exercises the legacy baseline-only proposer path; retrieval-aware harness invocation needs a follow-up loop integration
  - usage fields are evidence supplied by adapters and are not yet independently verified against provider billing
  - the compatibility adapter treats route as selected intent and rejects exhausted token/time allowance; provider adapters must add provider-specific usage verification
